{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJaMjjFao3c4qG1WeKU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MWvukZ8a8ArL69FnEcTmf4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-ewaz2U/memory/invoice-db-env-var.md","content":"---\nname: invoice-db-env-var\ndescription: Invoice service must read its DB connection string from INVOICE_DB_URL, never DATABASE_URL\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nThis service reads its database connection string from `INVOICE_DB_URL`, never from `DATABASE_URL`.\n\n**Why:** The deploy team settled this. On the host, `DATABASE_URL` points at the platform's shared database, so a service reading it would write invoices into that shared DB.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code, config, docs, tests, or docker/compose/CI files for this service, use `INVOICE_DB_URL`. Don't add a `DATABASE_URL` fallback or default either, since a fallback would silently reintroduce the problem.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9688,"cache_read_input_tokens":11962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9688,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8144567e-e2ad-4115-ad4e-3a830423043c","uuid":"e92e5277-5581-4cdf-90a7-09a27fc664db","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:29:07.458Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJaMdn548awdVsvgFtn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MWvukZ8a8ArL69FnEcTmf4":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-ewaz2U/memory/invoice-db-env-var.md","content":"---\nname: invoic